# --- Rust build output -----------------------------------------------------
/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Cargo.lock is COMMITTED on purpose. This workspace ships a binary
# (`crates/proxima-cli` -> `proxima`), and for a binary the lockfile is part of
# the build: it is what makes "the numbers in the docs are the numbers you get"
# true for someone who clones the repo. Do not add Cargo.lock here.

# --- Criterion ------------------------------------------------------------
# `cargo bench` writes its samples, estimates and reports under target/, but
# criterion also honours CRITERION_HOME, which people point at the repo root.
/criterion
criterion/
**/target/criterion/

# --- Proxima runtime artefacts --------------------------------------------
# The default data directory of `proxima serve` and `proxima query`.
proxima-data/
# WAL segments and snapshots, wherever a test or a local run drops them.
*.snap
wal
**/wal
*.wal

# --- Editors --------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- OS noise -------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
